# note: A losslessly compressed alpha plane carrying a palette transform,
#   from a cwebp encode of a two-valued plane.
# expect: ok
# roundtrip: no
# exercises: The one shape that reaches DecodeAlphaData(): exactly one
#   transform, that transform colour-indexing, no colour cache, and the red,
#   blue and alpha codes each a single symbol. That is the lossless decoder's
#   8-bit mode, a different loop from the one all 62 VP8L files here take, and
#   this is the only file in the corpus that runs it. Its partner alph-
#   lossless-predictor is the same feature failing the same test.
chunks VP8X ALPH VP8
alpha 1
alph_compression 1
alph_data 0f30ff111142209020ec6fb9440e11fdcf8909
width 16
height 16
yac_qi 30
macroblock
coeffs y2 -20
coeffs y[2] 1:5 -3
